title: >-
  rmt-llm-research — Random Matrix Theory meets Large Language Models:
  spectral analysis of activations and the mathematical inevitability
  of hallucinations
abstract: >-
  A research repository by Iskhak Hamzatovich Isaev applying Random Matrix
  Theory (RMT) to the analysis of large language models (LLMs). Three
  interconnected threads: (1) spectral statistics of LLM activations via
  Marchenko-Pastur law, BBP phase transition, and Tracy-Widom fluctuations;
  (2) ten independent mathematical paths converging on a single critical
  token count N_crit for hallucination onset (NHSE, Caputo fractional
  dynamics, EP-surfaces, Keating-Snaith, etc.); (3) the RLHF utility trap
  — Caputo memory parameter beta ≈ 0.5 makes <T_crit> ∝ (μ_eff)^(-1/β),
  quadratically accelerating hallucination onset under even small RLHF
  pressure. The repository ships 12 DOCX monographs (EN/RU), 1 PDF paper,
  a GitHub Pages documentation site, and an interactive in-browser demo.
